# Always Commit and Push

After completing a user-requested change, commit the relevant changes and push the current branch without waiting for a separate follow-up request.

- Questions such as “did you commit and push?” are also direct instructions to do so, not merely status requests.
- Stage only changes belonging to the current task; exclude unrelated files.
- Run proportionate checks before committing.
- Never force-push unless the user explicitly requests it.
- Stop and report if committing or pushing would be unsafe or is blocked.
- Report the commit and push result concisely.
